{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/443318-nautical-dead-domain-ideas","id":443318,"title":"Nautical dead domain ideas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T17:10:00-07:00","id":443318,"title":"Nautical dead domain ideas?","content":"The Ocean of Fragments is super cool, but it doesn't really work if you want a setting full of ghost pirates and grizzled dead sailors in Davy Jone's Locker- it's more of a final dungeon. So what kinds of Domains would you see being formed from the deaths of sailors? Are there aquatic sections of the Autocthonous Depths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:34:02-07:00","id":443952,"title":"","content":"I'd agree there are at least aquatic locations in the Upper Reaches, there is the Tear-Stained Key for those buried at sea or who somehow drowned after all and sections of the Underworld, as mentioned in Book of the Dead, take on aspects of common funeral practices in places, such as some parts of the Upper Reach being more like the inside of a furnace than a cave (complete with hotplate flooring and fire spurting through the walls) where people are commonly cremated rather than buried.<br /> I'd also say that that whatever this area would be, it'd link along to the Rivers, same as all Rivers lead to the Ocean of Fragments. One of the Admiral's Old Laws is that there is but one ocean and it's heavily hinted he is the leader of the seperate Ferrymen of the Rivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:40:34-07:00","id":443955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/443318-nautical-dead-domain-ideas#post443318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it's more of a final dungeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>try and read the OWoD books about Wraith. That'll quickly transform the ocean from a &quot;final dungeon&quot; to a hub-world of grotesque ocean themed shenanigans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:59:42-07:00","id":443966,"title":"","content":"Very true.<br /> Also, am I the only one that sees The Admiral as potentially the nwod version of Charon? Book of the Dead hinted to Orpheus being around in a more sinister MIB form, snatching away ghosts of people thought not to be dead, such as Elvis and Tupac... Plus the Maelstrom in Dark Eras, there's a few links to Wraith for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T10:12:43-08:00","id":1436034,"title":"","content":"Try the cenote, a massive pit of water where ghosts and people go to throw or offer things away. Laws: Never take anything that was thrown away. Don't pollute the Cenote. What comes up must come down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26513-laguz-24","name":"Laguz 24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26513_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}